From 8cb6e8629a590a988dfce2bddf83d5ed3536f7fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 17:30:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] software_isp: Plumb the aperture through to the soft
 IPA

Carry the iris lens's controls to the IPA and its chosen iris position
back, alongside the existing focus path. As with focus, the ControlInfoMap
is handed over at init() as well as configure(), so that an algorithm can
decide while registering controls whether an aperture exists at all.

The iris is passed as its own ControlInfoMap rather than merged into
lensControls. A ControlInfoMap only borrows its ControlIdMap, every V4L2
device owns its own, and the IPA keeps a copy of the map beyond the call,
so a merged map built from two sub-devices would leave a dangling idmap.
Keeping them separate also keeps the returned ControlLists valid, since a
ControlList is likewise tied to one idmap.

While here, only set V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE when the lens actually has
it. The old test was that the map was non-empty, which would set focus on
an iris-only lens.

Signed-off-by: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
